  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The current best (config_037: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, 0.706 acc) was reached by sequentially improving RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion strategy, all while holding aggregation at avgpool. The only untested dimension at this top level is aggregation: in RNA-only, avgpool (0.591) clearly outperformed transformer (0.519), but that was a unimodal setting. In multimodal, transformer aggregation could in principle capture richer cross-profile and cross-modal structure that simple averaging discards. config_039 is a clean single-variable change (avgpool→transformer) from the current best, so any performance difference is attributable solely to the aggregation choice. If transformer matches or exceeds avgpool, it opens a new optimization axis; if it underperforms (as expected from RNA-only evidence), it confirms avgpool as the optimal aggregation for multimodal fusion and closes that design dimension, freeing future budget for the remaining untested variable (scgpt RNA encoder). Under a tight budget, this is the highest-information, lowest-risk next step."
}

